# Markdown endings are pinned so a one-line edit can never show as a whole-file
# change. README.md and DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md were stored with CRLF, so any
# tool that wrote the file back with LF endings flipped every line into the repo:
# a zero-content rewrite showed as 2,203 changed lines, and it blocked a
# fast-forward on a two-line change. Storing and checking out LF in both
# directions fixes both, whichever way an editor writes the file.
#
# `text` is explicit rather than `auto`, which cannot recover a file already
# stored the wrong way. Binary files are unaffected.
*.md text eol=lf
